$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Compounds 9a-c, 10a-e, 11a-g, and
14 by Method C: General Procedure. A 5-mL process vial was charged with
the appropriate bromoindole derivative (1 mmol), the appropriate boronic
acid (5 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (22.5 mg, 0.1 mmol), PPh3 (78.6 mg, 0.3 mmol), 2
M Na2CO3 (2 mL, 4 mmol), EtOH (1 mL), and 1,2-dimethoxyethane (DME) (4
mL). The vessel was sealed under air and exposed to microwave heating for
10 min at 150 °C. The reaction mixture was thereafter cooled down to room
temperature, diluted with AcOEt, and filtered through a short plug of
Celite. The solution was washed with brine, dried over anhydrous sodium
sulfate, and evaporated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
on silica gel, eluted with DCM/MeOH (95:5).
N-(Adamantan-1-yl)-1-pentyl-5-(thiophen-2-yl)-1H-indole-3-carboxamide
(11f). 100% yield. White solid. Mp 214-217 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6)
δ 8.39 (s, 1H), 8.14 (s, 1H), 7.55-7.40 (m, 2H), 7.45 (d, J = 4.0 Hz,
1H), 7.39 (s, 1H), 7.11-7.07 (m, 2H), 4.16 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 2.10-2.06
(m, 9H), 1.79 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 1.67 (s. 6H), 1.34-1.24 (m, 4H), 0.85
(t, J = 8.0 Hz, 3H). IR (Nujol) 1638 cm-1. MS (ESI) m/z 447 [M+H]+, 469
[M+Na]+. Anal. (C28H34N2OS), C, H, N. Calcd.: C, 75.29; H, 7.67; N, 6.27.
Found C, 75.43; H, 7.56; N, 6.12.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, sealed vial used, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Synthesis, and Pharmacological Characterization of
Indol-3-ylacetamides, Indol-3-yloxoacetamides, and
Indol-3-ylcarboxamides: Potent and Selective CB2 Cannabinoid Receptor
Inverse Agonists
