$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure 1 for Boronation and Suziki
Coupling: To a dried flask were added 4-bromo-1-methyl-isatin (3.60 g, 15
mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron (4.07 g, 16 mmol), Pd(dppf)Cl2·CH2Cl2
(612.9 mg, 0.075 mmol, 5 mol%), KOAc (4.44 g, 45 mmol), dppf (166.0 mg,
0.3 mmol), and dioxane (150 mL) under a nitrogen atmosphere. The
resulting mixture was stirred at 100°C for 33 h, then filtered through
celite, washed with ethyl acetate, and evaporated to afford the crude
product. Following Typical Procedure 1, the reaction of
4-chloro-1-methyl-7-aza-indole (228.9 mg, 1.5 mmol),
bis(pinacolato)diboron (762.1 mg, 3 mmol), Pd(dppf)Cl2·CH2Cl2 (122.2 mg,
0.15 mmol, 10 mol%), and KOAc (441.3 mg, 4.5 mmol) in dioxane (12 mL).
1g-II (386.4 mg, quant.) (flash chromatograph eluent: hexane/ethyl
acetate = 2/1), which was used for next step directly.
