$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-((4aR,8R,8aR)-2,2-bis(1,1-dimethylethyl)-8-{[tris(1-methylethyl)silyl]oxy}-4,4a,8,8a-tetrahydropyrano[
3,2-d][1,3,2]dioxasilin-6-yl)-3-{[4-(1,1-dimethylethyl)phenyl]methyl}-1,2-benzisothiazole
(14d). To a solution of 12d (1 g, 2.78 mmol) and
(4aR,8R,8aR)-2,2-bis(1,1-dimethylethyl)-6-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-8-{[tris(1-methylethyl)silyl]oxy}-4,4a,8,8a-tetrahydropyrano[3,2-d][1,3,2]dioxasilin
13 (2.76 g, 4.86 mmol, WO 2005/012326, Chem Abstr 2005, 142, 219491) in
40 ml of 1,2-dimethoxyethane were added 2 M of sodium carbonate (15 ml)
and bis(triphenylphosphine) palladium(II) chloride (390 mg, 0.56 mmol).
The mixture was heated at 85 0C for 30 min and then cooled down. Ethyl
acetate was added and the organic layer was isolated. The organic layer
was washed with brine once and dried over magnesium sulfate. Column
chromatography with 0-10% ethyl acetate in hexane provided 14d as an oil
in quantitative yield, which proceeded directly to the next step.
