$DATUM 5-bromo-2-(methoxymethyl)pyridine (13.75 g, 68 mmol),
4,4,4',4',5,5,5',5'-octamethyl-2,2'-bi(1,3,2-dioxaborolane) (22.5 g, 89
mmol), potassium acetate (20.0 g, 204 mmol) and 1,1'-
bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocenedichloropalladium(II) (2.5 g, 3.4 mmol)
were suspended in dioxane (800 mL). The reaction was degased, purged with
N2 and heated to 85 °C for 4 hours. The mixture was then allowed to cool
to RT, filtered and evaporated. The residue was extracted with heptane
and filtered. The filtrate was evaporated to dryness.
2-(methoxymethyl)-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridine
as a yellow oil (24.3 g, >100%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, 303 K) 1.35
(12H, s), 3.47 (3H, s), 4.61 (2H, s), 7.42 (1H, s), 8.07 (1H, s), 8.88
(1H, s). m/z 250 (M+H)+.
