$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
arylpyridines and heteroarylpyridines To a solution of 2-bromopyridine 6
(0.5 g, 3.2 mmol) in toluene (12 ml), ethanol (2.3 ml) and H2O (12 ml)
was added Na2CO3 (2.5 g, 23.6 mmol) followed by Pd(PPh3)4 (0.1 g, 0.1
mmol) and 4-methylphenylboronic acid 5c (0.6 g 4.2 mmol) under Ar in 100
ml two-necked flask. The mixture was refluxed for 12 h, and then cooled
to room temperature. To the reaction mixture were added H2O and CH2Cl2.
The mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 three times, and the combined
organic layer was washed with sat. NaCl aq. and dried over MgSO4. After
removal of the solvent under reduced pressure, the residue was purified
by silica-gel column chromatography to give the compound 7c (0.6 g, 84%)
as a colorless oil. Spectral data were in good agreement with literature
values.4 7b, 7e, 7f, 7g, 7h, and 7i are known compounds. compound 7i,
yield 99%
