$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Suzuki-Miyaura Coupling: Method A:
Palladium (II) Encat™ BINAP(10 mol%, 0.30 mmol/g) was added to a mixture
of the aryl halide (1.0 eq), the boronate species (1.5 eq), and K2CO3
(3.0 eq) in ethanol:water (9:1, 1.0 M), the suspension was heated to 70
°C, and the reaction mixture was stirred at this temperature until
complete conversion was achieved as monitored by TLC and/or LC. The
reaction mixture was allowed to cool to rt. The solids were removed via
filtration, washed with dichloromethane (2×20 mL), and the combined
filtrates were concentrated in vacuo. The crude material was purified via
flash chromatography on silica to afford the desired product.
(2R)-4-(6-Methoxy-2'-oxo-3,4'-bipyridin-1'(2'H)-yl)-2-methyl-2-(methylsulfonyl)-N-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yloxy)butanamide
(16d). The title compound (240.6 mg, 100%) was obtained as a yellow solid
from
(2R)-4-(4-iodo-2-oxopyridin-1(2H)-yl)-2-methyl-2-(methylsulfonyl)-N-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yloxy)butanamide
(15) and 6-methoxy-3-pyridinylboronic acid using a procedure analogous to
that described in the General Suzuki-Miyaura Coupling, Method A. LCMS:
m/z 478.5 [M-H]-.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura coupling
