$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S)-2-amino-7'-(pyrimidin-5-yl)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2'-ol. A
pressure-vessel was charged with
(R)-2-amino-2'-bromo-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-7'-ol (15) (3.00 g,
8.64 mmol), pyrimidin-5-ylboronic acid (3.21 g, 25.9 mmol),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (1.00 g, 0.864 mmol),
tetrahydrofuran (43 mL), and potassium carbonate (21.60 mL, 43.2 mmol) (2
M aq. solution). The vessel was sealed under argon and placed in a 100°C
oil bath and stirred for 3 h. The mixture was poured into a separatory
funnel with the aid of EtOAc and a small amount of i-PrOH. The layers
were separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with 10%
i-PrOH/EtOAc. The combined organic layers were dried over sodium suflate,
filtered, and evaporated. The residue was taken up in DCM, sonicated and
filtered. This process was repeated twice.
(S)-2-amino-7'-(pyrimidin-5-yl)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthen]-2'-ol
(2.95 g, 8.52 mmol, 99 % yield) after airdrying. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d
6) δ ppm 9.42 (br. s., 1 H), 9.17 (s, 1 H), 9.07 (s, 2 H), 7.73 (dd,
J=8.5, 2.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.65 (d, J=2.2 Hz, 2 H), 7.25 (d, J=8.4 Hz, 1 H),
6.99 (d, J=8.5 Hz, 1 H), 6.70 -6.78 (m, 2 H), 6.43 (br. s., 2 H), 4.13
-4.24 (m, 2 H). MS m/z = 347.0 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed vessel used, pressure vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Lead Optimization and Modulation of hERG Activity in a Series of
Aminooxazoline Xanthene β-Site Amyloid Precursor Protein Cleaving Enzyme
(BACE1) Inhibitors
