$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 1. Sodium carbonate (1.6 g, 15 mmol) was added to
5-fluoro-2-methoxypyridin-4-ylboronic acid (1.0 g, 6.0 mmol) and
2,4-dichloropyrimidine (0.75 g, 5.0 mmol) in 4:1 dioxane/water (25 mL),
and the suspension was purged with argon. PdCl2(dppf)*DCM (0.21 g, 0.25
mmol) was added, and the mixture was heated at 80°C under argon
overnight. The reaction mixture was diluted with water, and the resulting
solid was collected by vacuum filtration, washed with water, and dried.
The desired 2-chloro-4-(5-fluoro-2-methoxypyridin-4-yl)pyrimidine (1.2 g,
99% yield) as a solid. m/z (APCI-pos) M+1 = 240.1, 242.0.
