$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(1-Methylindol-2-yl)quinoline (5fh). Under argon atmosphere, a reaction
tube was charged with palladium salt (Pd(OAc)2 (2.25 mg, 0.01 mmol) or
[Pd(allyl)Cl]2 (1.83 mg, 0.005 mmol)), imidazolium salt 2d (8.66 mg, 0.02
mmol) and cesium carbonate (652 mg, 2 mmol). Then, dioxane (2 mL) was
added. The mixture was stirred for 15 min at 90 °C and cooled to room
temperature. (This precatalyst formation was essential for high catalytic
performance.) Then, heteroaryl chloride 3 (1.0 mmol) and
(hetero)arylboron reagent 4 (1.5 mmol) were added. The reaction mixture
was stirred for 18 h at 90 °C and cooled to room temperature. Water and
saturated Na2CO3 were added and then the resulting mixture was extracted
with ether. The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4.
Concentration and purification through silica gel column chromatography
gave desired product 5 4-(1-Methylindol-2-yl)quinoline (5fh). After the
reaction mixture was stirred for 18 h at 100 °C and cooled to room
temperature, CH2Cl2 and 1M NaOH were added. The resulting mixture was
stirred for 1 h at room temperature and extracted with CH2Cl2. The
combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4. Concentration and
purification through silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc =
5/1) gave the product 4-(1-Methylindol-2-yl)quinoline (5fh). White
solids, 256 mg, (0.99 mmol, 99%). mp 174-175 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3):
3.57 (3H, s), 6.72 (1H, s), 7.22 (1H, t, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.34 (1H, t, J =
8.0 Hz), 7.43-7.45 (2H, m), 7.53 (1H, t, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.72 (1H, d, J =
7.6 Hz), 7.76 (1H, t, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.84 (1H, d, J = 8.0 Hz), 8.21 (1H, d,
J = 8.0 Hz), 9.01 (1H, d, J = 4.4 Hz). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): 31.1
(CH3), 104.4 (CH), 109.7 (CH), 120.2 (CH), 120.9 (CH), 122.4 (CH), 122.8
(CH), 126.1 (CH), 127.2 (CH), 127.6 (C), 127.8 (C), 129.6 (CH), 129.9
(CH), 136.4 (C), 138.2 (C), 139.1 (C), 148.5 (C), 149.8 (CH). IR (ATR):
800, 1500, 1590 cm-1. HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C18H14N2 (M+): 258.1157.
Found: 258.1152.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
