$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bis(5-triisopropylsilyl-3,3'-bithiophen-2-yl)acetylene (5a).
Bis(3-bromo-5-triisopropylsilyl-2-thienyl)acetylene 7a (3.96 g, 6.02
mmol), 3-thiopheneboronic acid (2.30 g, 18.0 mmol), Pd2(dba)3·CHCl3 (126
mg, 0.122 mmol), 2-(2',6'-dimethoxybiphenyl)dicyclohexylphosphine
(S-Phos) (99.8 mg, 0.243 mmol), and K3PO4 (5.12 g, 24.2 mmol) were placed
in a 100 mL three-necked flask, which was degassed twice and filled with
argon. Anhydrous toluene (60 mL) was added to the mixture. After the
solution was stirred at 110 °C for 20 h, the mixture was allowed to cool
down to room temperature. After filtration and washing with CH2Cl2, the
organic solvents were removed under reduced pressure. The mixture was
purified by silica gel column chromatography (hexane, Rf = 0.27) to
afford 5a. Bis(5-triisopropylsilyl-3,3'-bithiophen-2-yl)acetylene (5a),
(3.89 g, 5.84 mmol), 97% yield, white solid Mp. 103–104 °C; 1H NMR
(CDCl3): δ 7.79 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 2H, Th-H), 7.59 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 2H,
Th-H), 7.34 (s, 2H, Th-H), 7.33 (dd, J1 = 4.8 Hz, J2 = 2.4 Hz, 2H, Th-H),
1.37 (septet, J = 7.6 Hz, 6H, TIPS-H), 1.15 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 36H, TIPS-H);
13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 140.1, 138.1, 136.3, 135.7, 127.4, 125.6, 122.5,
122.4, 91.3, 18.7, 11.9; HRMS (APCI, positive): 666.2346 (M+), calcd for
C36H50S4Si2: 666.2328.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Sequential Electrophilic and Photochemical Cyclizations from
Bis(bithienyl)acetylene to a Tetrathienonaphthalene Core
